Four guard objects cl does not have - ?Identity@?$Consts@UTag1@@@@2UR@@B$guard and its neighbours. cl runs a template static member's constructor from a COMDAT initialiser function of its own, ??__E...@@YAXXZ, and the linker's folding is what makes it run once; ml64 cannot mark a COMDAT, so cxx1 guards the construction with a weak flag beside the object instead, the way both compilers already do on the Itanium targets. See template-static-data-member-ctor.nonames.
